war and includes the sentence: \\'The whole nation is united in its resolve.\\' The article has no byline. Which statement best evaluates what this source can address?\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"allowed_actions\": [\\n            \"select-many\",\\n            \"select-one\"\\n          ],\\n          \"approved_item_id\": \"dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:146999b6-55f9-44f0-908e-ae511be23ada.i3\",\\n          \"evidence_ref\": \"item.dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:146999b6-55f9-44f0-908e-ae511be23ada.i3\",\\n          \"kind\": \"multiple_choice\",\\n          \"stem\": \"A letter written by a soldier on 12 October 1917 to his parents describes conditions in the trenches and states: \\'The officers have no idea what we are going through.\\' Which statement best explains how the author\\'s identity and situation shape what the letter can address?\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"allowed_actions\": [\\n            \"select-many\",\\n            \"select-one\"\\n          ],\\n          \"approved_item_id\": \"dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:146999b6-55f9-44f0-908e-ae511be23ada.i4\",\\n          \"evidence_ref\": \"item.dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:146999b6-55f9-44f0-908e-ae511be23ada.i4\",\\n          \"kind\": \"multiple_choice\",\\n          \"stem\": \"A shop\\'s ledger from 1850 lists daily sales and includes a note: \\'Business is failing because of the new tariff.\\' The ledger is signed only \\'The Proprietor.\\' Which statement best describes the authorship context and what the source can address?\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"allowed_actions\": [\\n            \"select-many\",\\n            \"select-one\"\\n          ],\\n          \"approved_item_id\": \"dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:146999b6-55f9-44f0-908e-ae511be23ada.i5\",\\n          \"evidence_ref\": \"item.dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:146999b6-55f9-44f0-908e-ae511be23ada.i5\",\\n          \"kind\": \"multiple_choice\",\\n          \"stem\": \"A poster from 1943 states: \\'Buy war bonds\\\\u2014every purchase protects a soldier.\\' The poster is issued by a government agency but no individual author is named. Which statement best evaluates what this source can address?\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"eligible_intents\": [\\n        \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"apply\",\\n        \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"classify\",\\n        \"compare\",\\n        \"connect-back\",\\n        \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"interpret\",\\n        \"orient\",\\n        \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"sequence\"\\n      ],\\n      \"forbidden_terminology\": [],\\n      \"required_assessment_slots\": [\\n        \"check\"\\n      ],\\n      \"rules\": {\\n        \"action_must_be_from_bound_source_allowed_actions\": true,\\n        \"copy_evidence_refs_verbatim\": true,\\n        \"copy_ids_verbatim\": true,\\n        \"item_kind_is_fixed_upstream\": true,\\n        \"multiple_choice_ids_per_block\": \"0_or_1\",\\n        \"response_action_requires_approved_source\": true,\\n        \"reuse_across_blocks\": \"forbidden\",\\n        \"source_only_in_required_assessment_slots\": true,\\n        \"source_only_on_eligible_intent\": true,\\n        \"source_requires_learner_action\": true\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \"instruction\": \"Return the complete corrected TeachingPlan JSON. Change only fields required to satisfy these errors. Use only intents listed under slot_intent_policy for each slot. Treat assessment_source_policy as a closed contract: copy approved_item_id and evidence_ref strings verbatim; never construct or concatenate IDs. Bind sources only inside required_assessment_slots when that list is non-empty. Every bound source must have a learner_action whose action appears in that source\\'s allowed_actions. Do not emit an unbound response-bearing learner_action. Keep optional guided or independent practice passive when no structurally planned approved source belongs there. Remove forbidden terminology and use only allowed_evidence_refs.\",\\n    \"legality_catalogue_hash\": \"c0250ed98d2f5abca69c19e4cc866ed36f855b8b33ad2c4fdd12ed3ba64db415\",\\n    \"previous_output\": {\\n      \"anchor_usage\": [\\n        {\\n          \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n          \"usage\": \"Open on the two accounts of the same event and set their conflicting statements side by side as the puzzle the lesson must resolve.\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n          \"usage\": \"Use the two accounts as the standing instance while establishing the four features (author, date, type, purpose) and how each narrows what the source can address.\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n          \"usage\": \"Return to the two accounts and run the four features across both, so the boundary is visible in a single pair rather than in two unrelated examples.\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n          \"usage\": \"No use of the anchor: the check uses a fresh, previously unseen source so that success depends on the method, not on recall of the opening pair.\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"arc\": \"The lesson opens on two first-hand accounts of the same event that disagree in what they can be used to prove, and uses that disagreement to raise the question of which features of a source control what it can address. It then establishes that author, date, type, and purpose (stated or implied) are four features that must each be read off the source and that together bound its usable claim. Students compare the two accounts feature by feature, confront the three beliefs that a first-hand source is unqualified evidence, that type alone fixes purpose, and that an unknown author means no limitation, and close by naming those four features and their consequences on a fresh source.\",\\n      \"misconception_focus_ids\": [\\n        \"M1\",\\n        \"M2\",\\n        \"M3\"\\n      ],\\n      \"sections\": [\\n        {\\n          \"blocks\": [\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Present the two first-hand accounts of the same event and the specific claim each one makes about it, showing that the two claims cannot both be used the same way as evidence about what happened. Do not name author, date, type, or purpose as analytical categories yet, and do not explain why the two accounts differ. The only job here is to put the disagreement on the table and make the learner want to know what is doing the work.\",\\n              \"departure_reason\": null,\\n              \"evidence\": \"The objective is to describe how author, date, type, and purpose shape what a source can address, so the lesson must first put the learner in front of two sources that differ in exactly what they can address; without a felt puzzle, the four features are a list to memorise rather than a tool to reach for.\",\\n              \"evidence_refs\": [\\n                \"anchor.anchor-1\",\\n                \"lesson.objective\",\\n                \"slot.orient.purpose\"\\n              ],\\n              \"intent\": \"orient\",\\n              \"learner_action\": null,\\n              \"source_question_ids\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_needs\": [\\n                \"Two short first-hand accounts of one event, by different authors, with identifiable date and type for each.\"\\n              ],\\n              \"sourcebook_refs\": [],\\n              \"stimulus_dependencies\": [\\n                \"anchor-1\"\\n              ],\\n              \"task_mode\": \"none\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Recall, in two or three lines, that a primary source is a first-hand account by someone who was there, and that such accounts of the same event can differ. Do not yet say what causes the difference or what limits a source. The recall is the platform the next section stands on.\",\\n              \"departure_reason\": null,\\n              \"evidence\": \"The lesson\\'s whole mechanism is that first-hand status is necessary but not sufficient, so the prior beliefs that a primary source is first-hand and that such accounts vary must be on the table and explicitly available before the explanation can complicate them.\",\\n              \"evidence_refs\": [\\n                \"prior-1\",\\n                \"prior-2\",\\n                \"slot.orient.purpose\"\\n              ],\\n              \"intent\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n              \"learner_action\": {\\n                \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n                \"difficulty\": \"guided\",\\n                \"expected_evidence\": \"Learner selects the statement that a primary source is first-hand and that first-hand accounts can differ\",\\n                \"purpose\": \"Confirm the prior concept the lesson will build on is active before it is complicated\",\\n                \"target\": \"which of two short statements correctly describes a primary source and whether two first-hand accounts of one event can differ\"\\n              },\\n              \"source_question_ids\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_needs\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_refs\": [],\\n              \"stimulus_dependencies\": [],\\n              \"task_mode\": \"formative\"\\n            }\\n          ],\\n          \"specific_purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n          \"transition\": null\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"blocks\": [\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Name the four features that must be read off any primary source: author (who created it and what their role or position was), date (when it was produced), type (what kind of account it is), and purpose (what the author was trying to do \\\\u2014 stated openly or merely implied by the wording). Use the first of the two accounts to point at each feature in turn, and state clearly that these four are identified from the source itself, not assumed from its subject. Do not yet show what each feature rules in or out.\",\\n              \"departure_reason\": null,\\n              \"evidence\": \"The objective requires the learner to identify author, date, type, and purpose, and those four elements are exactly the constituent parts the learner must be able to locate before any consequence can be stated; naming them on a real instance prevents them from being an abstract four-word list.\",\\n              \"evidence_refs\": [\\n                \"lesson.objective\",\\n                \"slot.explain.purpose\",\\n                \"anchor.anchor-1\"\\n              ],\\n              \"intent\": \"name-parts\",\\n              \"learner_action\": null,\\n              \"source_question_ids\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_needs\": [\\n                \"The first of the two accounts from the opening, with author, date, type, and purpose each identifiable from the source.\"\\n              ],\\n              \"sourcebook_refs\": [],\\n              \"stimulus_dependencies\": [\\n                \"anchor-1\"\\n              ],\\n              \"task_mode\": \"none\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Establish the causal chain from feature to usable claim: because the author occupied a particular position on a particular day, and because the type of account was written to do a particular job, the account can speak with authority to some questions and cannot speak to others. Work it through on the first account: its author\\'s position gives it access to some facts and not others, and its implied purpose pulls its language toward one framing. State plainly that identifying a source as first-hand does not exempt it from this chain. Do not evaluate the source or call it biased; the point is what it can address, not whether it is fair.\",\\n              \"departure_reason\": null,\\n              \"evidence\": \"M1 holds that first-hand status makes every factual statement usable, so the lesson must supply the causal link it is missing \\\\u2014 a feature of the author or the act of writing restricting what the account can address \\\\u2014 before any confrontation can land.\",\\n              \"evidence_refs\": [\\n                \"lesson.objective\",\\n                \"slot.explain.purpose\",\\n                \"misconception-1\",\\n                \"anchor.anchor-1\"\\n              ],\\n              \"intent\": \"explain-cause\",\\n              \"learner_action\": null,\\n              \"source_question_ids\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_needs\": [\\n                \"The first account\\'s author role, date, type, and implied purpose, plus one question the account is well placed to answer and one it is not.\"\\n              ],\\n              \"sourcebook_refs\": [],\\n              \"stimulus_dependencies\": [\\n                \"anchor-1\"\\n              ],\\n              \"task_mode\": \"none\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Set out the second account against the first on the same four features, so the learner sees that the same event can be addressed from a different angle because the features differ. Make explicit that purpose is a consequence of the author\\'s role and situation at the moment of writing, not of the type: two accounts of the same type can carry different purposes, and two accounts of different types can carry the same purpose. Do not re-derive the causal chain already stated; use it.\",\\n              \"departure_reason\": null,\\n              \"evidence\": \"M2 holds that type alone fixes purpose, so the explanation must place the two accounts\\' purposes side by side and tie each to the author\\'s role rather than to the label of the account, otherwise the learner can keep reading purpose off the category.\",\\n              \"evidence_refs\": [\\n                \"lesson.objective\",\\n                \"slot.explain.purpose\",\\n                \"misconception-2\",\\n                \"anchor.anchor-1\"\\n              ],\\n              \"intent\": \"explain\",\\n              \"learner_action\": null,\\n              \"source_question_ids\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_needs\": [\\n                \"The second account\\'s author role, date, type, and implied purpose, contrasted with the first.\"\\n              ],\\n              \"sourcebook_refs\": [],\\n              \"stimulus_dependencies\": [\\n                \"anchor-1\"\\n              ],\\n              \"task_mode\": \"none\"\\n            }\\n          ],\\n          \"specific_purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n          \"transition\": \"Learners now hold a genuine conflict between two first-hand accounts and know that first-hand status alone does not settle it, so they are ready for the four features that do.\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"blocks\": [\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Run the four features across the two anchor accounts feature by feature \\\\u2014 author, then date, then type, then purpose \\\\u2014 and for each feature state one question the account can address and one it cannot. The learner must see that the two accounts differ on what they can address even though both are first-hand, and that the differences track the features, not the first-hand status. Do not restate the general causal chain or the list of features as a definition; apply them.\",\\n              \"departure_reason\": null,\\n              \"evidence\": \"The two accounts differ on some features and agree on others, so a feature-by-feature comparison is the only move that shows which feature is responsible for which limit; a general restatement would leave the learner unable to attribute a limit to a feature.\",\\n              \"evidence_refs\": [\\n                \"anchor.anchor-1\",\\n                \"slot.contrast.purpose\",\\n                \"lesson.objective\"\\n              ],\\n              \"intent\": \"compare\",\\n              \"learner_action\": {\\n                \"action\": \"classify-items\",\\n                \"difficulty\": \"guided\",\\n                \"expected_evidence\": \"Each question is assigned to the account whose author, date, type, and purpose actually give it access to that question\",\\n                \"purpose\": \"Force the feature-to-limit link to be used, not just recognised\",\\n                \"target\": \"three short questions about the event, sorted by which of the two accounts can properly address each\"\\n              },\\n              \"source_question_ids\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_needs\": [\\n                \"A four-feature breakdown of both anchor accounts with one addressable and one unaddressable question per feature.\"\\n              ],\\n              \"sourcebook_refs\": [],\\n              \"stimulus_dependencies\": [\\n                \"anchor-1\"\\n              ],\\n              \"task_mode\": \"formative\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Put up a confident claim of the form \\'this account is first-hand and the author was present, so we can use its statement about X as evidence that X happened,\\' and show the claim failing when the author\\'s position and the account\\'s implied purpose are checked. The failure must be visible from the features, not asserted. Do not explain the general reason first-hand status is insufficient again; the explanation has already been given, so here it is only tested against a claim a learner could plausibly make.\",\\n              \"departure_reason\": null,\\n              \"evidence\": \"M1 is a held belief, not a slip, and the contrast slot is the point where a confident wrong claim can be written and dismantled using the two accounts already in play; the misconception is only displaced when the learner watches the inference collapse on a case they have already accepted.\",\\n              \"evidence_refs\": [\\n                \"misconception-1\",\\n                \"anchor.anchor-1\",\\n                \"slot.contrast.purpose\"\\n              ],\\n              \"intent\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n              \"learner_action\": {\\n                \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n                \"difficulty\": \"guided\",\\n                \"expected_evidence\": \"Learner rejects the claim on a feature-based reason rather than on a general doubt about sources\",\\n                \"purpose\": \"Surface and test the belief that first-hand status alone licenses the use\",\\n                \"target\": \"whether a stated first-hand claim about the event can be used as evidence about that event, and why\"\\n              },\\n              \"source_question_ids\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_needs\": [\\n                \"A first-hand source statement that reads as usable evidence but is restricted by the author\\'s position or the implied purpose.\"\\n              ],\\n              \"sourcebook_refs\": [],\\n              \"stimulus_dependencies\": [\\n                \"anchor-1\"\\n              ],\\n              \"task_mode\": \"formative\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Put up a second confident claim that a source with no named individual author, issued by an institution, has no authorship context and therefore no limit on what it can address. Show that the issuing body, the date, and the implied purpose still constrain what it can address, and that absence of a personal name removes access to the author\\'s specific position but not the limitation. Keep this distinct from the earlier block: that one was about first-hand status, this one is about unnamed authorship.\",\\n              \"departure_reason\": null,\\n              \"evidence\": \"M3 is a separate wrong model \\\\u2014 it treats anonymity as the absence of limitation \\\\u2014 so it needs its own test; collapsing it with the first-hand belief would leave the anonymous-source case unaddressed while the learner believes it is already covered.\",\\n              \"evidence_refs\": [\\n                \"misconception-3\",\\n                \"slot.contrast.purpose\",\\n                \"lesson.objective\"\\n              ],\\n              \"intent\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n              \"learner_action\": {\\n                \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n                \"difficulty\": \"guided\",\\n                \"expected_evidence\": \"Learner states a limitation grounded in the issuing body, date, or implied purpose rather than in the missing name\",\\n                \"purpose\": \"Surface the belief that no name means no authorship context\",\\n                \"target\": \"whether an unsigned institutional source can still be limited in what it can address, and on what grounds\"\\n              },\\n              \"source_question_ids\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_needs\": [\\n                \"A short institutional or unsigned source with a date and an evident purpose but no named individual author.\"\\n              ],\\n              \"sourcebook_refs\": [],\\n              \"stimulus_dependencies\": [],\\n              \"task_mode\": \"formative\"\\n            }\\n          ],\\n          \"specific_purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\",\\n          \"transition\": \"The four features and their causal link are on the table, so learners can now test where the link holds and where a tempting shortcut fails.\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"blocks\": [\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"On a source not used earlier in the lesson, require the learner to identify author, date, type, and stated or implied purpose and to state what each feature lets the source address and what it rules out. Both a feature-listing answer and a feature-consequence answer must be distinguishable, so that selecting the better description is diagnostic of whether the objective landed.\",\\n              \"departure_reason\": null,\\n              \"evidence\": \"The check slot is the lesson\\'s only measurement point and the objective names both identification and consequence, so the item must be one where the correct description of authorship context and what the source can address is separable from a description that only names features.\",\\n              \"evidence_refs\": [\\n                \"lesson.objective\",\\n                \"slot.check.purpose\",\\n                \"item.dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:146999b6-55f9-44f0-908e-ae511be23ada.i4\"\\n              ],\\n              \"intent\": \"check-understanding\",\\n              \"learner_action\": {\\n                \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n                \"difficulty\": \"independent\",\\n                \"expected_evidence\": \"Learner selects the description that ties the ledger\\'s unsigned authorship and commercial purpose to a specific limit on what the ledger can address\",\\n                \"purpose\": \"Measure whether the learner can read the four features off an unseen source and state the resulting limit on what it can address\",\\n                \"target\": \"the statement that best describes the authorship context of the ledger and what the source can address\"\\n              },\\n              \"source_question_ids\": [\\n                \"dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:dcb318ad-494a-4ffc-8dff-292ff6723dad:146999b6-55f9-44f0-908e-ae511be23ada.i4\"\\n              ],\\n              \"sourcebook_needs\": [],\\n              \"sourcebook_refs\": [],\\n              \"stimulus_dependencies\": [],\\n              \"task_mode\": \"assessment\"\\n            }\\n          ],\\n          \"specific_purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\",\\n          \"transition\": \"The learner has identified the four features on the anchor pair and seen a first-hand claim and an anonymous-source claim fail, so they are ready to apply the same reasoning unaided to a source they have not seen.\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"slot_intent_policy\": {\\n      \"check\": {\\n        \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n        \"permitted_departures\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"memory-aid\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"warn\"\\n        ],\\n        \"typical_intents\": [\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"practise-independent\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"contrast\": {\\n        \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n        \"permitted_departures\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"memory-aid\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"trace-flow\"\\n        ],\\n        \"typical_intents\": [\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"warn\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"explain\": {\\n        \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n        \"permitted_departures\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"memory-aid\",\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"warn\"\\n        ],\\n        \"typical_intents\": [\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"trace-flow\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"orient\": {\\n        \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n        \"permitted_departures\": [\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"memory-aid\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"warn\"\\n        ],\\n        \"typical_intents\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"orient\"\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \"validation_errors\": [\\n      \"INTENT_LEGALITY: intent \\'diagnose-misconception\\' is atypical for this slot and requires departure_reason\",\\n      \"INTENT_LEGALITY: intent \\'diagnose-misconception\\' is atypical for this slot and requires departure_reason\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"slot_intent_policy\": {\\n    \"check\": {\\n      \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n      \"permitted_departures\": [\\n        \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"apply\",\\n        \"classify\",\\n        \"compare\",\\n        \"connect-back\",\\n        \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"define\",\\n        \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"derive\",\\n        \"emphasise\",\\n        \"explain\",\\n        \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"interpret\",\\n        \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"name-parts\",\\n        \"orient\",\\n        \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"sequence\",\\n        \"show-structure\",\\n        \"summarise\",\\n        \"trace-flow\",\\n        \"warn\"\\n      ],\\n      \"typical_intents\": [\\n        \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"practise-independent\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"contrast\": {\\n      \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n      \"permitted_departures\": [\\n        \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"apply\",\\n        \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"connect-back\",\\n        \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"define\",\\n        \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"derive\",\\n        \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"emphasise\",\\n        \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"interpret\",\\n        \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"name-parts\",\\n        \"orient\",\\n        \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"sequence\",\\n        \"summarise\",\\n        \"trace-flow\"\\n      ],\\n      \"typical_intents\": [\\n        \"classify\",\\n        \"compare\",\\n        \"explain\",\\n        \"show-structure\",\\n        \"warn\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"explain\": {\\n      \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n      \"permitted_departures\": [\\n        \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"apply\",\\n        \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"classify\",\\n        \"connect-back\",\\n        \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"derive\",\\n        \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"emphasise\",\\n        \"interpret\",\\n        \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"orient\",\\n        \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"sequence\",\\n        \"summarise\",\\n        \"warn\"\\n      ],\\n      \"typical_intents\": [\\n        \"compare\",\\n        \"define\",\\n        \"explain\",\\n        \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"name-parts\",\\n        \"show-structure\",\\n        \"trace-flow\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"orient\": {\\n      \"departure_rule\": \"A permitted non-typical intent requires a specific departure_reason. Excluded intents are never legal.\",\\n      \"permitted_departures\": [\\n        \"apply\",\\n        \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"classify\",\\n        \"compare\",\\n        \"connect-back\",\\n        \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"define\",\\n        \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"derive\",\\n        \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"explain\",\\n        \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"interpret\",\\n        \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"name-parts\",\\n        \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"sequence\",\\n        \"show-structure\",\\n        \"summarise\",\\n        \"trace-flow\",\\n        \"warn\"\\n      ],\\n      \"typical_intents\": [\\n        \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"emphasise\",\\n        \"orient\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \"teaching_guidance\": {\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"intents\": [\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Prompt recall of concepts required for this lesson. Keep it brief and diagnostic.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Surface prerequisite knowledge\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Require selection and use of the learned idea in a recognizable context.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"apply\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Use knowledge in a familiar situation\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The teacher needs to know right now whether the objective landed, and correct-versus-incorrect is the signal being read.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'diagnose-misconception\\': \\'wrong answers must identify WHICH wrong model the learner holds\\', \\'practise-independent\\': \\'the purpose is rehearsal rather than measurement\\', \\'reflect\\': \\'there is no correct answer\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Detect immediate misunderstanding\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Provide or elicit a rule for category membership and contrast borderline cases.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"classify\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Organize examples into categories\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Two or more named things must be told apart, and the same criteria apply to each.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"compare\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'classify\\': \\'instances are being sorted by a rule rather than two things contrasted\\', \\'diagnose-misconception\\': \\'one side is a wrong belief, not a legitimate alternative\\', \\'evaluate\\': \\'one option must be judged better, not merely distinguished\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Expose similarities and differences\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Show which prior idea is being reused and exactly how it supports the current task.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"connect-back\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Make prerequisite dependence explicit\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"State what the current idea enables next and the unresolved question that follows.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Bridge current learning to the next idea\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Give a precise learner-appropriate definition, distinguish it from nearby terms, and include notation only when useful.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"define\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Establish precise meaning\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner has not yet seen the method carried out end to end on a real instance, and the method is unambiguous once seen. If the learner has already seen it worked through in this lesson, this condition is no longer met.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'model-thinking\\': \\'the difficulty is choosing between approaches, not executing one\\', \\'derive\\': \\'the result must be justified from prior statements, not computed\\', \\'practise-guided\\': \\'the learner is attempting the work, not watching it\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Model a complete method\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The result must be shown to FOLLOW from statements the learner already accepts, and each transformation needs a stated justification.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"derive\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'demonstrate\\': \\'the point is the procedure, not its justification\\', \\'model-thinking\\': \\'steps are chosen from alternatives rather than compelled\\', \\'explain-cause\\': \\'the chain is physical rather than logical\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Build a result from prior statements\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"A named, real misconception exists on the card, and a wrong answer can be written that only a learner holding it would confidently choose. One block per misconception the card declares \\\\u2014 a misconception not on the card does not exist.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'check-understanding\\': \\'no specific wrong model is known; the check only detects failure\\', \\'warn\\': \\'the error is a slip or lapse, not a held belief\\', \\'compare\\': \\'both sides are legitimate\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Distinguish a known wrong model from the target model\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Set apart only the single statement learners should retain. Do not create multiple competing key ideas.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"emphasise\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Mark a high-value statement\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Require criteria, evidence, a judgment, and limitations.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"evaluate\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Judge a claim, method, or evidence\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner must reason about instances they have not seen, and the difficulty is the idea itself \\\\u2014 not its cause, its flow, its arrangement, or a representation of it.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"explain\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'explain-cause\\': \\'the objective asks WHY, and a mechanism links cause to result\\', \\'trace-flow\\': \\'something is followed as it moves or changes through a system\\', \\'show-structure\\': \\'the difficulty is arrangement, containment, or hierarchy\\', \\'interpret\\': \\'a specific representation is on the page and must be read\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Build a coherent mental model\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The objective asks why, or what happens if, and there is a mechanism between cause and result that the learner must be able to state.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'explain\\': \\'there is no cause-and-effect chain, only meaning or structure\\', \\'trace-flow\\': \\'the emphasis is on what moves, not on what causes\\', \\'sequence\\': \\'order matters but no causal mechanism does\\', \\'derive\\': \\'the chain is logical rather than physical\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Connect causes, mechanisms, and outcomes\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Explain what a graph, formula, diagram, table, or result means in context.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"interpret\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Translate representation into meaning\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Specify question, variables, observations, and evidence expectations. Avoid pretending a screen simulation is a paper practical.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"investigate\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Structure an inquiry or practical\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Provide a short, accurate cue that does not replace understanding.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Support recall with a compact cue\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"State why each decision is made, what alternatives were rejected, and what signal triggered the next step.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"model-thinking\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Expose expert decision making\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Identify the important parts of a system or idea and state each part\\'s role.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"name-parts\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Identify constituent elements\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Begin with a concrete phenomenon, dilemma, observation, or question. Do not explain the full idea yet.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"orient\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Open attention and establish a reason to learn\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner can begin the task but will stall without prompts, partial steps, or hints.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'practise-independent\\': \\'support would now be a crutch\\', \\'demonstrate\\': \\'the learner is watching rather than attempting\\', \\'apply\\': \\'the point is first unaided use, not scaffolded rehearsal\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Rehearse with structured support\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner has already succeeded with support and must now perform unaided, with enough repetition for fluency.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'practise-guided\\': \\'the learner has not yet succeeded with support\\', \\'check-understanding\\': \\'the purpose is measurement, not rehearsal\\', \\'transfer\\': \\'the context is deliberately changed\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Rehearse without scaffolding\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Ask learners to explain what changed in their thinking, what remains difficult, or which strategy helped.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"reflect\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Prompt learners to examine their understanding\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Express steps or events in a meaningful order. Include dependencies and stopping conditions where relevant.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"sequence\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Represent an ordered process\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Show levels, containment, arrangement, or relationships that are hard to infer from prose.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"show-structure\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Reveal spatial or hierarchical organization\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"State what the learner should be able to explain, do, compare, or justify.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"state-goal\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Clarify the expected learning outcome\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Restate the minimum complete model, not a list of disconnected facts.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"summarise\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Compress the lesson into essential relationships\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Something identifiable \\\\u2014 matter, energy, information, money, data \\\\u2014 enters, changes, moves, and leaves, and the learner must not lose track of it.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"trace-flow\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'sequence\\': \\'the steps are actions taken, not a substance being followed\\', \\'explain-cause\\': \\'the point is why it happens, not where it goes\\', \\'show-structure\\': \\'the arrangement is static and nothing travels through it\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Follow matter, energy, information, or value\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Change surface features enough that learners must recognize the underlying structure.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"transfer\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Use knowledge in a changed context\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"A specific error is predictable at this exact point, and naming it before it happens prevents it.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"warn\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'diagnose-misconception\\': \\'the error is a held belief that must be surfaced and tested, not a slip to flag\\', \\'emphasise\\': \\'the content is a positive statement to retain, not an error to avoid\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Prevent a predictable error\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"projection_hash\": \"a9530874d702efc409dcd4c87658fe037981b8a8a6ed76e1d95a551ff8885870\"\\n  }\\n}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
