unts of the same event, three wrong beliefs feel convincing. Test each against the accounts themselves.\\\\n\\\\n1. \\\\\"If a source doesn\\'t name its writer, it has no author and can be treated as neutral.\\\\\" It feels right because an unnamed source looks impartial \u2014 no name, no side. But an unidentified author is an unknown position, not a neutral one. The account that never names its writer still reveals a point of view in what it includes and what it leaves out. Ask who might have written it and what that person would have had reason to report or omit.\\\\n\\\\n2. \\\\\"A source written closer in time is automatically more reliable, and the date alone settles what it can be used for.\\\\\" It feels right because being close to the event sounds like better access. But a date close to the event limits the source to immediate observation \u2014 it cannot speak to later consequences. The later account can address remembered experience and reflection that the earlier one cannot. So the date shapes what each source can address; it does not rank them once and for all.\\\\n\\\\n3. \\\\\"Purpose counts only if the source states it; with no written purpose, the source can be read as a plain record.\\\\\" It feels right because an unstated purpose is not on the page. But purpose can often be identified from what the source asks its readers to do and from what it suppresses. One of the source accounts carries a purpose it never names.\\\\n\\\\nCorrect position: an unnamed author, a given date, and an unstated purpose each still shape what the source can address. None of them removes the need to ask the four questions \u2014 who wrote it, when, what type of source it is, and its stated or implied purpose.\"\\n}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '1 validation error:\\n```json\\n[\\n  {\\n    \"type\": \"missing\",\\n    \"loc\": [\\n      \"response\"\\n    ],\\n    \"msg\": \"Field required\"\\n  }\\n]\\n```\\n\\nFix the errors and try again.'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 8000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
