{"timestamp": "2026-09-16T16:18:38.701227+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-012a14ec-84b3-4616-a1cb-a10bd10e1397', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You prepare the educational structure of one approved lesson.\\n\\nThe path owns the objective and concept identity. The skeleton supplies a strong\\nrecommended sequence and a closed legal slot catalogue. You may select the exact\\npedagogical sequence for this objective, but code validates the result.\\nA later planner will choose page blocks. You must not choose components, page\\nobjects, layouts, or question text.\\n\\n## FIXED INPUT\\n\\n- objective and objective_hash\\n- concept_id\\n- primary_knowledge_type\\n- lesson_mode\\n- recommended_slots and legal_slots with slot purposes\\n- hard_constraints including max_slots, required visuals, and verification\\n- scope_contract\\n- prior_established\\n- explicit prerequisites\\n- lesson_actuals\\n- carried anchor, when present\\n- resource identity and purpose\\n\\n## YOUR DECISIONS\\n\\n1. Draft zero to three real misconceptions. Each must support a confident wrong\\n   answer. A missing term is a knowledge gap, not a misconception.\\n2. Reuse the carried anchor when it fits. Otherwise choose one concrete anchor\\n   and state why it is new.\\n3. Choose selected_slots from legal_slots. Keep the recommendation when it fits;\\n   every meaningful departure needs flow_rationale and flow_departures.\\n4. Give each selected section a concise title and transition note. Return exactly\\n   one semantic section payload per selected slot, in selected order.\\n   The first section\\'s transition_note must be null; only later sections\\n   may explain how they follow the preceding section.\\n4. Do not output technical identity. The backend attaches objective, concept id,\\n   section id/role, card_id, and visual_required after your response.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n- Never output or rewrite the objective or concept ID.\\n- Never invent a slot role, exceed max_slots, remove required visual work, or\\n  remove the final verification/check capability.\\n- Never choose a component, page object, pedagogical block intent, placement,\\n  or visual form.\\n- Never write question text.\\n- Never reteach prior_established in the structural rationale.\\n- Never introduce must_not_introduce content.\\n- Never manufacture a misconception to fill a count.\\n- Never choose page blocks, intents, objects, or briefs. A later planner\\n  owns the teaching design.\\n\\nIf the objective cannot honestly fit the legal slot catalogue, emit deviation_request.\\nIf the objective itself is wrong, emit objective_concern. Do not repair either.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only, matching the supplied output schema.\\n\\nThe output contains only:\\n\\n- anchor as {\"description\": str, \"source\": \"carried\"|\"new\"}\\n- one semantic concept-card payload (title/prereqs/misconceptions/opens_by;\\n  no id or objective)\\n- selected_slots, flow_rationale, and flow_departures\\n- sections with title and transition_note only, one per selected slot in order\\n- deviation_request or null\\n- objective_concern or null\\n\\nIt contains no components and no blocks.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n1. Did I avoid outputting upstream-owned identity/objective fields?\\n2. Are selected_slots legal, bounded, and verification-complete?\\n3. Did I return exactly one section payload per selected slot, in order?\\n4. Does every misconception pass the confident-wrong-answer test?\\n5. Did I choose any page form or teaching block? Remove it.\\n6. Did I contradict prior_established, terminology, or exclusions?\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"FlowDeparture\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"operation\": {\"enum\": [\"insert\", \"remove\", \"replace\", \"reorder\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"from_slot\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"to_slot\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"reason\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"operation\", \"reason\"], \"title\": \"FlowDeparture\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathAnchor\": {\"properties\": {\"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source\": {\"enum\": [\"carried\", \"new\"], \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"description\", \"source\"], \"title\": \"PathAnchor\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathDeviationRequest\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"operation\": {\"enum\": [\"insert\", \"remove\", \"replace\", \"reorder\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"target_slot\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"replacement_slot\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"operation\", \"target_slot\", \"replacement_slot\", \"reason\"], \"title\": \"PathDeviationRequest\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralMisconception\": {\"properties\": {\"id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"description\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"The wrong belief, stated the way a learner would state it.\"}, \"statement\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"source\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralMisconception\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralPageCard\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"title\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"prereqs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"misconceptions\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralMisconception\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"no_known_misconceptions\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"opens_by\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralPageCard\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralPageSection\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"title\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"transition_note\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"title\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralPageSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"anchor\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathAnchor\"}, \"cards\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralPageCard\"}, \"maxItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralPageSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"selected_slots\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"flow_rationale\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"flow_departures\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FlowDeparture\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"deviation_request\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathDeviationRequest\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"objective_concern\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"anchor\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralPagePlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"concept_id\": \"e7d78449-b105-4a9e-986f-1a1af2290134\",\\n  \"exclusions\": [],\\n  \"external_prerequisites\": [],\\n  \"group_ids\": [],\\n  \"groups\": [],\\n  \"hard_constraints\": {\\n    \"required_visual_slots\": [],\\n    \"verification_required\": true\\n  },\\n  \"legal_slots\": [\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Reactivate the specific prior knowledge this lesson depends on. Nothing else.\",\\n      \"role\": \"recall\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"recall\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Show the method being carried out, with each step\\'s reasoning visible.\",\\n      \"role\": \"model\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"model\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n      \"role\": \"explain\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Name the wrong belief, show why it feels right, then show it failing on a case. Correct exposition alone does not count.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"confront\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"confront\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Impose a structure on the facts so they are retrievable, not just listed.\",\\n      \"role\": \"organise\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"organise\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Establish what a good answer is judged against, before any case is seen.\",\\n      \"role\": \"criteria\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"criteria\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Practice with scaffolding still present. Learner does the thinking, support stays.\",\\n      \"role\": \"guided\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"guided\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Practice with scaffolding removed.\",\\n      \"role\": \"independent\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"independent\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Use the idea on a context not seen in this lesson.\",\\n      \"role\": \"apply\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"apply\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": true,\\n      \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"check\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Consolidate what was established and name what comes next.\",\\n      \"role\": \"close\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"close\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"lesson_actuals\": [],\\n  \"max_slots\": 6,\\n  \"must_establish\": [\\n    \"State the central claim of each source in a single sentence expressed as something the source asserts about the event.\",\\n    \"Distinguish a source\\'s central claim from supporting details, examples, or background it provides.\",\\n    \"Match each supporting detail in a source to the claim it is offered to support.\"\\n  ],\\n  \"native_whole_lesson\": true,\\n  \"objective\": \"Extract and state the central claims each of two primary-source accounts makes about the same event, distinguishing claims from supporting detail\",\\n  \"objective_hash\": \"2c014b6cc65a5e14dd25d76c8efb3271f17d8ccd99af8521e174b55855d338d9\",\\n  \"prerequisites\": [\\n    {\\n      \"concept_id\": \"146999b6-55f9-44f0-908e-ae511be23ada\",\\n      \"objective\": \"Identify the author, date, type, and stated or implied purpose of two given primary-source accounts and describe how each of these features shapes what the source can address\",\\n      \"path_lesson_id\": \"c08f7d6d-49ab-458b-a595-d70eef5c9d3b\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"primary_knowledge_type\": \"conceptual\",\\n  \"prior_established\": [\\n    \"a primary source is a first-hand account created by someone who witnessed or took part in an event\",\\n    \"primary sources reflect the perspective and limits of their author, so accounts of the same event can differ\",\\n    \"read a short historical source and identify its author, date, and main claim\",\\n    \"For each source, name its author, or state that the author is unknown, and note the author\\'s role or position relative to the event.\",\\n    \"For each source, state its date and whether it is contemporary with the event or written later.\",\\n    \"For each source, describe its stated or inferred purpose (e.g., to report, persuade, record, commemorate).\",\\n    \"Explain how an author\\'s role, date, or purpose narrows or expands the kinds of claims the source can speak to.\"\\n  ],\\n  \"recommended_slots\": [\\n    \"orient\",\\n    \"explain\",\\n    \"contrast\",\\n    \"check\"\\n  ],\\n  \"scope_contract\": {\\n    \"assumed_prerequisites\": [],\\n    \"may_include\": [],\\n    \"must_establish\": [\\n      \"identify the author, date, and stated purpose of each primary-source account and explain how that context shapes what the source can say\",\\n      \"identify the specific claims each primary-source account makes about the same event\",\\n      \"evaluate each source\\'s usefulness for supporting a given claim using relevant criteria (authorship, position, proximity, purpose, corroboration)\",\\n      \"justify which claims each source can support by referring to the source\\'s own evidence and limitations\"\\n    ],\\n    \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n      \"historiographical schools of interpretation or theory of history\",\\n      \"source criticism of documents in languages other than English\"\\n    ],\\n    \"notation\": null,\\n    \"terminology\": [\\n      \"primary source\",\\n      \"claim\",\\n      \"evidence\",\\n      \"author\",\\n      \"date\",\\n      \"purpose\",\\n      \"perspective\",\\n      \"bias\",\\n      \"corroboration\",\\n      \"limitation\",\\n      \"support\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"secondary_demand\": null,\\n  \"shared_preparation\": true,\\n  \"slots\": [\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n      \"role\": \"explain\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"locked\": true,\\n      \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"check\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"title\": \"Extracting claims from each account\",\\n  \"variant_previews\": [\\n    {\\n      \"group_profile\": \"core\",\\n      \"slots\": [\\n        {\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n          \"role\": \"orient\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n          \"role\": \"explain\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n          \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"locked\": true,\\n          \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n          \"role\": \"check\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"toggles_applied\": [\\n        \"misconception.confront_per_belief\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
