 one that gives a supporting reason or fact, and the claim sentence. Contrast them on the single criterion of whether the sentence asserts something the writer is putting forward for the reader to accept. Make clear that all three are true statements about the same passage, so truth alone does not decide it, and that the topic sentence and the supporting fact are doing different jobs than the claim.\",\\n      \"evidence\": \"The contrast slot must expose the boundary of the idea, and the two most likely wrong candidates are the topic sentence and the supporting fact; comparing them with the claim on the acceptance criterion is what makes that boundary visible rather than asserted.\",\\n      \"id\": \"contrast-b1\",\\n      \"intent\": \"compare\",\\n      \"sourcebook_refs\": []\\n    },\\n    \"terminology\": [\\n      \"claim\",\\n      \"evidence\",\\n      \"relevant evidence\",\\n      \"irrelevant detail\",\\n      \"support\"\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nReturn JSON only for this capability payload.'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"properties\": {\"response\": {\"additionalProperties\": true, \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"required\": [\"response\"], \"type\": \"object\", \"title\": \"dict\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Return JSON only for the selected capability payload.'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 8000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
