 situation to hold.\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Reactivate the specific prior knowledge this lesson depends on. Nothing else.\",\\n      \"role\": \"recall\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"recall\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Show the method being carried out, with each step\\'s reasoning visible.\",\\n      \"role\": \"model\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"model\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n      \"role\": \"explain\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Name the wrong belief, show why it feels right, then show it failing on a case. Correct exposition alone does not count.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"confront\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"confront\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Impose a structure on the facts so they are retrievable, not just listed.\",\\n      \"role\": \"organise\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"organise\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Establish what a good answer is judged against, before any case is seen.\",\\n      \"role\": \"criteria\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"criteria\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Practice with scaffolding still present. Learner does the thinking, support stays.\",\\n      \"role\": \"guided\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"guided\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Practice with scaffolding removed.\",\\n      \"role\": \"independent\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"independent\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Use the idea on a context not seen in this lesson.\",\\n      \"role\": \"apply\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"apply\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": true,\\n      \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"check\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Consolidate what was established and name what comes next.\",\\n      \"role\": \"close\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"close\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"lesson_actuals\": [],\\n  \"max_slots\": 6,\\n  \"must_establish\": [\\n    \"vertical change is the difference in y-coordinates between two points\",\\n    \"horizontal change is the difference in x-coordinates between two points\",\\n    \"rise and run can be positive or negative depending on the order of subtraction\"\\n  ],\\n  \"native_whole_lesson\": true,\\n  \"objective\": \"identify the vertical change (rise) and horizontal change (run) between two ordered pairs on the coordinate plane\",\\n  \"objective_hash\": \"2618b60e4cd2a2bfcd956f483e4eb96cc559024b40f44e5a41c6aed53ed79c6f\",\\n  \"prerequisites\": [],\\n  \"primary_knowledge_type\": \"conceptual\",\\n  \"prior_established\": [\\n    \"read and plot coordinate pairs on the coordinate plane\",\\n    \"read values off a graphed line\",\\n    \"identify the x- and y-coordinates of a point\"\\n  ],\\n  \"recommended_slots\": [\\n    \"orient\",\\n    \"explain\",\\n    \"contrast\",\\n    \"check\"\\n  ],\\n  \"scope_contract\": {\\n    \"assumed_prerequisites\": [],\\n    \"may_include\": [],\\n    \"must_establish\": [\\n      \"calculating slope from two points using the slope formula\",\\n      \"interpreting slope as a unit rate of vertical change per horizontal change\",\\n      \"recognizing slope sign (positive, negative, zero) from two points\",\\n      \"applying slope to compare or describe steepness of lines\"\\n    ],\\n    \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n      \"deriving the slope-intercept form y = mx + b from two points\",\\n      \"finding the equation of a line through two points\",\\n      \"slopes of parallel and perpendicular lines\",\\n      \"slope of a line from a table with non-consecutive rows using formulas beyond slope\"\\n    ],\\n    \"notation\": null,\\n    \"terminology\": [\\n      \"slope\",\\n      \"rise\",\\n      \"run\",\\n      \"vertical change\",\\n      \"horizontal change\",\\n      \"unit rate\",\\n      \"steepness\",\\n      \"positive slope\",\\n      \"negative slope\",\\n      \"zero slope\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"secondary_demand\": null,\\n  \"shared_preparation\": true,\\n  \"slots\": [\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n      \"role\": \"explain\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n